blocks.en:
Ego–Action–World interactions are the unit of organization. Each interaction is represented by three components.
The Ego captures the wearer’s interaction-relevant state, including observations, goals, and current subgoals;
the Action captures executed behavior and its progress;
and the World captures external entities, their states, and state changes.
Together, these components provide a common representation for organizing diverse egocentric understanding capabilities.
Related interactions can further be grouped into task episodes to capture dependencies beyond a single event.

blocks.zh:
Ego-Action-世界互动是组织单位. 每个互动由三个组成部分代表。
Ego捕捉穿行者的互动相关状态,包括观察、目标和目前的分目标;
行动抓住已执行的行为及其进展;
和世界捕捉 外部实体, 它们的状态, 和州的变化。
这些组成部分共同为组织各种自我中心理解能力提供了共同的代表。
相关互动可以被进一步分组为任务集,以捕捉单个事件之外的依赖性.
